   "text": "The modern Smalltalk-80\nCuis is a free Smalltalk-80 environment with a specific set of goals: being simple and powerful .\nIt is also portable to any platform , fast and efficient.\nGet started\nA typical work-in-progress scene in Cuis Smalltalk application development: An Inspector displays an object from the running application, a message is sent to this object to show its halo, and the auto-completion tool is active. Class browsers are open on the application’s relevant classes; a Transcript provides feedback on the application’s execution; under the application view, a Workspace contains code related to the application.\nA showcase of Cuis Smalltalk’s support for vector graphics, SVG, TrueType fonts and Unicode.\n“I like it… It’s nice and clean and simple and pretty. Nice stuff!”\n2007-04-27 · Source\n“Yay, Juan. You GO, guy! …a great example of malleable software (and a clever mind) at work.”\n2007-04-27 · Source\n“I think you have a very elegant design aesthetic.”\n2007-11-19 · Private communication\nMore nice comments about Cuis\nLatest news\n2026-10-01\nCuis at Smalltalks 2026\nSmalltalks 2026 takes place from October 14 to 16 at the Facultad Regional Rosario of the UTN, in Rosario, Argentina, and Cuis will be there: eight talks of the program come from the Cuis community or show work done in Cuis. We hope to see you all there!\n2026-06-02\nJuly Cuis Meeting\nWhat. It is a “Demo Meeting” for demonstration then discussion.\nMilan Lajtos will present his experience on using a code agent to\ndevelop Blueprint, a revisit of the Cuis Smalltalk system desktop.\n2026-06-01\nCuis 7.8 release\nCuis 7.8 stable release!\nOlder news\nSubscribe\nLatest meeting\nWebsite, Dybo and Stream Deck\nCristián Pérez presents the redesigned website and Cuis for Stream Deck , his new plugin for controlling Cuis from a Stream Deck. Hilaire Fernandes shows the improvements to the Dybo tools.\nCristián Pérez & Hilaire Fernandes\n2026-10\nPast meetings"
